From 41e0382594a4575aa694151fe60e8bfb39c348f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiran Kunigiri <kirankunigiri@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:44:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fill screens squarer than 3:2 (foldables, tablets) in IB2 and
 IB3

On a near-square screen (e.g. a foldable's inner display) both games
kept a 3:2 or 16:9 3D view with big black bars above and below.

- app.cpp: give IB2 the window's shape when it is squarer than 3:2
  (with the Full screen setting), as IB3 already gets.
- widescreen.cpp, both games: SwordCamera only gives the view the
  screen's shape when bIsWideAspectRatio (InitializeFor: aspect > 1.5);
  the threshold becomes 0.5 and UpdateViewTarget's FOV scaling becomes
  FMax (same-size tokens), so the view fills the screen with the 3:2
  field of view and more above and below.
- IB2: AdjustHUDRenderSize's 1.7 bound is lowered too so the HUD
  covers the screen; menu backdrops are scaled for the taller view.
- IB3: the HUD keeps its own 3:2 iPad layout (laying it over the whole
  screen misplaces the move circles away from where they take taps);
  RenderIPadBars' two 80-high bars become 0 high and the exploring
  vignette is skipped. Served through devipa.cpp's SwordGame.xxx copy,
  which owns that file for IB3.
- Each game falls back to its stock layout if the patterns are not found.

Tested on a 2480x2248 screen: IB2 world, cutscene, menus, character
screen, fight; IB3 cutscenes, exploring, fight (move tap, block).
